  "notes": [
   "The catalog prints subject abbreviations that differ from the closed list: PSYC-104 = PSYCH 104, PSYC-235 = PSYCH 235, COMM-260 = COMS 260, POLS-290 = POLISC 290. Same numbers and titles, so they are treated as closed-list courses (catalog_addition false). A reviewer should confirm this.",
   "POLS-290 is printed as 'Ethics and Gender Politics'; the closed list title is 'Ethnic and Gender Politics'. SOCI-107 is printed as 'Introduction to Chicana/o Studies' in the requirements and as 'Culture' in the course description. SOCI-130 is printed as 'Introduction to LGBT+ Studies' in this section.",
   "SOCI-200H is printed on its own line without 'OR' in both choice lists. It is recorded as the honors alternative of SOCI-200.",
   "The 'seven to eight units' block requires SOCI-102 AND one statistics course (PSYC-104 or SOCI-137 or STAT-C1000/C1000E/C1000H). It is recorded as an all-required block with stated 7-8.",
